cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "Paying for Outcomes Is an Adjudication Problem: A Reference Design for Outcome-Based Pricing of AI Agents (RFC 0001, v0.1)"
authors:
  - family-names: Sasson
    given-names: Dor
    affiliation: Stigg
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  Outcome-based pricing for AI agents stalls because nobody trustworthy decides
  what counted as an outcome. This RFC proposes a reference design: success
  specifications compiled from the planned task, a four-tier decision cascade
  that puts facts before opinions, pinned and calibrated deciders that act as the
  contract's definition of an outcome, and an append-only outcome ledger, with a
  contracted overbilling bound and pre-registered predictions.
keywords:
  - outcome-based pricing
  - AI agents
  - agent evaluation
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - conformal prediction
  - reward hacking
  - usage-based billing
  - revenue recognition
  - metering
